id: pm-utxk3h
title: Preserve telemetry events across concurrent queue rewrites
description: "Live backend correlation for a bounded invocation window found 102 complete pairs and one comments finish without its start. Pairing used installation, process session, canonical command, and the finish started_at timestamp. The local event queue was empty and did not retain that start. Source inspection shows process-local mutation serialization around queue rewrites; cross-process append-versus-rewrite loss is a hypothesis requiring deterministic reproduction."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-13T09:41:11.342Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-13T23:36:35.433Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-13T23:36:34.248Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-13T23:36:34.248Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce missing lifecycle events with isolated concurrent processes and a local collector; preserve events across append, successful flush, retry, retention pruning, and span rewriting; verify paired production probes and exact coverage without weakening consent or timeout guarantees"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make event delivery completeness independently verifiable under concurrent CLI use
value: Trustworthy action histories beyond aggregate success rates
parent: pm-5oj5
resolution: Preserve concurrent event/span queue transactions and cold identity; isolate collector fixture credentials and document transaction boundaries
expected_result: Concurrent lifecycle events survive rewrites and loopback tests cannot inherit production ingest credentials
actual_result: "Synthetic credential regression, independent-process pairing, full 8832 tests at exact coverage, and packed npm/Bun acceptance pass; local timing limitation and reviewer quotas are explicitly recorded"
